  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Clear skies with warming trend this week.\n\n\nDespite the cold temperatures experienced this morning, afternoon \nhighs are expected to be warmer than yesterday. The warmest \ntemperatures today will reach into the upper 50s and may scratch 60 \nin parts of the Piedmont. A surface high pressure system will \nget closer and stay in the NRV and keep skies mostly clear and \nwinds calm for the rest of the week. This will result in a \nlarge range of diurnal temperatures followed by an overall \nwarming trend into the weekend. Tonight's temperatures will be \nwarmer along the Blue Ridge and other elevated areas for the \nnext few nights as the center of a 850mb high carrying \nrelatively warmer temperatures settles in. In addition, \ntonight's temperatures may not be as cold as yesterday but lower\nPWATs, calm winds, and clear skies will still result in cold \ntemperatures reaching as low as the upper 20s to lower 30s \noutside of the Blue Ridge. As the week progresses and heights \nincrease, temperatures will get unseasonably warm for this time \nof year. By Friday, low temperatures may be in the mid-30s to \nmid-40s and highs may be in the 60s areawide. No other \nsignificant weather changes are likely until this weekend when \ncloud cover increases from a frontal system that may pass \nthrough.",
